We finished eating.
We stepped outside the restaurant.
The rain has reduced now.
The streets have filled with water.
Prakash called an auto.
We waited for the auto.
Anitha and Deepa talked and laughed.
They have quickly become good friends.
My neighbor and coworkers stood together.
That gave me a lot of happiness.
After a while, Prakash and Deepa's auto arrived.
"Good night, Maya," Deepa said.
"Once again, happy birthday," Prakash also said.
They both got in it and left.
Anitha and I got another auto.
We headed back home in that auto.
A cold wind blew outside.
I have now turned thirty-two.
This city has now become my own place.
